{
  "spec": "CONTROL.md §14.7 (the level), §1: nothing is ever auto-allowed",
  "note": "A run gets the narrowest of the rule's level, the machine's mode (where `inherit` lets a named level be `safe` at most) and, continuing a session, that session's own recorded level. A notice rule is `edits` at most: a rules file that has one wider is refused whole, read as no rules and triggers off. A triggered run answers no permission prompt: a prompt it raises is left to the harness, which denies it at `safe` and `edits`.",
  "cases": [
    {
